%N A086261 Number of antisymmetric n X n conference matrices.
%C A086261 Antisymmetric conference matrices of order n are in bijection with skew Hadamard matrices and therefore with labeled doubly-regular tournaments on n-1 vertices [Reid and Brown]. Thus, a(n) = 2^{n-1} * Sum_T ((n-1)! / |Aut(T)|), where T runs over unlabeled DRTs. A catalog of DRTs is given by McKay. - _Andrei Zabolotskii_, Aug 23 2026
%H A086261 Brendan McKay, <a href="https://users.cecs.anu.edu.au/~bdm/data/digraphs.html#:~:text=doubly%2Dregular">Digraphs. Regular and Semi-regular Tournaments</a>.
%H A086261 K. B. Reid and Ezra Brown, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/0097-3165(72)90098-2">Doubly regular tournaments are equivalent to skew Hadamard matrices</a>, Journal of Combinatorial Theory, Series A, 12 (1972), 332-338.
%H A086261 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/C-Matrix.html">C-Matrix</a>
